  "footnote": "No prerequisites to the major. The eight CAPS courses total 30-36 credits and require a grade average of C or better; the app does not check the average. Complete three years of college-level Chinese (CHIN 1000-level through 3000-level) and attain high-intermediate proficiency or higher. Language sequencing and proficiency are reviewed outside the checklist. Native speakers with regular high school diplomas from mainland China or Taiwan (not international schools), or students exempted through placement testing, may receive a language exemption at Chinese language faculty discretion with CAPS administrator approval. Take a placement test before Beijing and expect to be at least at the 3000 level then. One semester of CAPS study abroad in Beijing is required, normally in junior or senior year. The Washington, D.C. semester is optional; consult the Director of Undergraduate Studies. Optional honors requires CAPS 4010 and CAPS 4020 while writing a thesis; together they may fulfill one CAPS elective, not two. The app cannot enforce that paired substitution. ENGL 2860 or ENGL 2880 used for FWS cannot also count toward the major.",
